From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:57:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Respect null values in DataFrame
 ElementwiseEquals/ElementwiseNotEquals

PrimitiveDataFrameColumn comparisons compared the raw buffer values and
ignored the validity bitmap, so a null (stored as default(T)) compared
equal to 0. ElementwiseEquals/ElementwiseNotEquals now decide rows where
an operand is null by validity only: null == null is true, null == value
is false (and the inverse for NotEquals). This applies to column/column
and column/scalar comparisons, including mixed column types.

Fixes #6820
---
 ...imitiveColumnContainer.BinaryOperations.cs | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../PrimitiveDataFrameColumnTests.cs          | 38 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+)

